---
source: crates/rustman-cli/src/tests.rs
expression: help
---
Publish messages (a kind: amqp request, or --value flags, or the lines of a piped stdin) with publisher confirms

Usage: rustman amqp produce [OPTIONS] [REQUEST]

Arguments:
  [REQUEST]
          A request file, its id or its name; without one, the flags describe the operation

Options:
      --broker <URL>
          The broker URL: amqp:// or amqps://

      --exchange <NAME>
          The exchange (default: the default exchange)

      --routing-key <KEY>
          The routing key

      --mandatory
          Fail when no queue is bound for the routing key

      --value <TEXT>
          A message value (repeatable); without one, each line of a piped stdin is a message

  -H, --header <NAME: VALUE>
          Add a header to every message (repeatable): --header "source: cli"

      --json
          Print one JSON object per message

      --env <NAME>
          Environment (default: RUSTMAN_ENV, then default_environment)

      --workspace <DIR>
          Workspace directory (default: search from the current directory upwards)

      --var <K=V>
          Set a variable, above every other source (repeatable): --var k=v

      --no-history
          Do not record the operation in history

      --color <WHEN>
          Color: auto (a terminal without NO_COLOR or TERM=dumb), always or never
          
          [default: auto]

  -v, --verbose...
          Log more on stderr: -v requests, -vv headers, -vvv everything (RUST_LOG, when set, replaces these levels)

  -h, --help
          Print help
